description: Find and coordinate evidence-based duplicate reduction
---

Treat `$ARGUMENTS` as the code target, not a Beads scope. Resolve it to the requested path(s); ask only if missing or ambiguous. Scan only that target, using the repository root only when the whole project is requested.

Run local jscpd with the managed config and compact reporter:

```sh
jscpd --config "$HOME/.config/opencode/jscpd.json" --reporters ai --no-tips --fail-on-empty -- "<resolved-target>"
```

Replace the placeholder with the resolved path; for multiple targets, pass each as a separate quoted argument. Keep the managed exclusions and local-only detection: do not substitute project configuration, use MCP or remote analysis services, or enable embeddings or downloads.

Read reported source fragments and nearby context as needed to judge worthwhile changes. Report clone locations, actual scope and material limitations, including excluded code, unavailable cross-target matches, scan failures, empty analysis or truncated output. Do not treat incomplete results as a complete scan.

Recommend reduction only where it simplifies genuinely equivalent behavior; retain intentional repetition with a reason and flag uncertain candidates. No worthwhile change is a valid outcome. Suggest follow-up work only when useful. Do not edit code, create a Bead unless explicitly asked, or launch execution.
